/bin (Binary Directory)
Contains basic commands used in terminal

/boot
Contains files required for system booting
Includes kernel and bootloader files

/dev
Contains files for hardware devices

/etc
Stores system configuration files, it is one of the most important directories in Linux

/home
personal folders for users

/lib (Library Directory)
Contains shared libraries for system programs and binaries
 
/root
Home directory for the root (admin) user
Not the same as /
Only accessible with admin privileges
